A timeout can limit waiting while leaving a large result problem intact. Limit query results explicitly and choose a bounded consumption path.

Book basis: [B4](/lore/durability-bibliography#b4-release-it).

## Failure it prevents

One query exhausts memory despite a concurrency limit of one.

## Our Effect 4.0.0 reading

`Stream.take` bounds consumption of a real stream. It cannot undo a driver’s full allocation. Apply limits or cursor pagination in the query [adapter](/lore/hexagonal-architecture).

Source: `packages/effect/src/Stream.ts`.

## How to check

Use a dataset larger than the intended result budget. Check rows fetched and memory before consumption completes. This check is our proposal. The books do not prescribe it.

Continue with [Steady state recycles resources](/lore/steady-state-recycles-resources), [Bulkheads isolate scarce capacity](/lore/bulkheads-isolate-capacity).

